{"name":"Stone Quarry","hex":"#ece4dc","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"stone","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard earthen substance that can form rocks; especially, such substance when regarded as a building material.","A piece of such material: a block of stone, rock or a pebble."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Constructed of stone.","Having the appearance of stone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stone"},{"term":"quarry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A site for mining stone, such as limestone, or slate."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To obtain (or mine) stone by extraction from a quarry.","To extract or slowly obtain by long, tedious searching."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quarry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Quarry","blocks":[{"text":"A quarry is a place where rock and earth materials – such as limestone, marble, granite, gravel, and sand – are excavated. The operation of quarries is regulated in some jurisdictions to manage their safety risks and reduce their environmental impact."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/PortlandQuarry.jpg/330px-PortlandQuarry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quarry","wikidata":"Q188040"},{"title":"Rock (geology)","blocks":[{"text":"In geology, a rock is any naturally occurring solid mass or aggregate of minerals or mineraloid matter. It is categorized by the minerals included, its chemical composition, and the way in which it is formed. Rocks form the Earth's outer solid layer, the crust, and most of its interior, except for the liquid outer core and pockets of magma in the asthenosphere. The study of rocks involves multiple subdisciplines of geology, including petrology and mineralogy. It may be limited to rocks found on Earth, or it may include planetary geology that studies the rocks of other celestial objects."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Marsh_Butte_and_Geikie_Peak%2C_Grand_Canyon.jpg/330px-Marsh_Butte_and_Geikie_Peak%2C_Grand_Canyon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_(geology)","wikidata":"Q8063"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Stone_quarry_adelaide.JPG/500px-Stone_quarry_adelaide.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Stone_quarry_adelaide.JPG/1280px-Stone_quarry_adelaide.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Stone_quarry_adelaide.JPG/500px-Stone_quarry_adelaide.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An abandoned construction aggregate quarry near Adelaide, South Australia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStone_quarry_adelaide.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Sulfureuse_vir%C3%A9e.jpg/500px-Sulfureuse_vir%C3%A9e.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Sulfureuse_vir%C3%A9e.jpg/1280px-Sulfureuse_vir%C3%A9e.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Sulfureuse_vir%C3%A9e.jpg/500px-Sulfureuse_vir%C3%A9e.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An abandoned construction aggregate quarry with turquoise pond near Thouars, France","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASulfureuse_vir%C3%A9e.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Stone_Quarry_Kerala.JPG/500px-Stone_Quarry_Kerala.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, htt